{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevArgmax","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.KashaevArgmax","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevProdEndpoint"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_le_argmax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_le_argmax","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevArgmax.lean#L203-L232","doc":"**The largest Kashaev term is at `k = ⌊5N/6⌋`** — the discrete saddle.\n`θ* = k*π/N` is within `π/N` of the solution of `2 sin θ = 1` in `(π/2, π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.one_le_kashaevProd_argmax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.one_le_kashaevProd_argmax","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevArgmax.lean#L186-L201","doc":"**`1 ≤ kashaevProd N ⌊5N/6⌋`.**  The sequence falls from `k*` to `N−1`,\nwhere it equals `N²` exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_le_of_falling_small","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_le_of_falling_small","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevArgmax.lean#L171-L182","doc":"Falling run near `j = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_le_of_falling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_le_of_falling","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevArgmax.lean#L156-L169","doc":"Falling run past the saddle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_le_of_rising","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_le_of_rising","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevArgmax.lean#L142-L154","doc":"Rising run: `kashaevProd N a ≤ kashaevProd N b` when every step between\nlands in the rising window. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_succ_le_of_large","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_succ_le_of_large","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevArgmax.lean#L121-L138","doc":"Falling step, past the saddle: `5N ≤ 6(k+1)` and `k+1 ≤ N` put\n`(k+1)π/N` in `[5π/6, π]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_succ_le_of_small","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_succ_le_of_small","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevArgmax.lean#L103-L119","doc":"Falling step, near `j = 0`: `6(k+1) ≤ N` puts `(k+1)π/N` in `(0, π/6]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_le_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_le_succ","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevArgmax.lean#L88-L101","doc":"Rising step: `N ≤ 6(k+1) ≤ 5N` puts `(k+1)π/N` in `[π/6, 5π/6]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_succ","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevArgmax.lean#L78-L86","doc":"**`kashaevProd N (k+1) = kashaevProd N k · (2 sin((k+1)π/N))²`.**\nThe whole argument is this identity plus where `2 sin` crosses `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sin_le_half_of_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sin_le_half_of_ge","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevArgmax.lean#L70-L74","doc":"`sin θ ≤ 1/2` on `[5π/6, π]`, by reflection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sin_le_half_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sin_le_half_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevArgmax.lean#L62-L68","doc":"`sin θ ≤ 1/2` on `[0, π/6]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.half_le_sin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.half_le_sin","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevArgmax.lean#L49-L60","doc":"`sin θ ≥ 1/2` on `[π/6, 5π/6]`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}